.TH REYNARD 1 "2025-11-22" "Reynard 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
reynard \- terminal-based xBase/FoxPro 2.x environment (the clever fox of terminals)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B reynard
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ script.prg ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reynard is a cross-platform, terminal-based reimplementation of the FoxPro
2.x/xBase environment for Linux, BSD, and macOS. With no arguments it opens
the full-screen interactive environment (System menu bar, Command window,
status line). With a script argument, or
.BR \-c ,
it runs the same interpreter in batch mode; with
.B \-t
the batch is deterministic (DATE(), TIME(), RAND() frozen to a session
seed) for use in test harnesses.
Commands worth knowing beyond the language docs (docs/language.md):
BUILD PROJECT name FROM file.rpj builds a .RPP package + launcher;
SET PROCEDURE TO file.prg|app.rpp loads procedure sources; ON KEY LABEL key
cmd binds a key (F1 opens the help DBF browser otherwise); SET HELP TO
file.dbf selects the help table; BEGIN/END TRANSACTION and ROLLBACK provide
journaling (see docs/DEVIATIONS.md).

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c " \fIcmd; cmd\fR"
Run commands then exit (batch). Semicolons split commands in this argument
only.
.TP
.B \-t
Test mode: deterministic batch.
.TP
.BI \-o " file"
Redirect batch stdout to
.IR file .
.TP
.BI --run " app.rpp"
Run a packaged application built by BUILD PROJECT (spec 9.6): executes the
packed main program from its compiled blob, with packed sources available to
DO and packed res/ and data/ extracted onto SET PATH. See docs/formats.md 8.
.TP
.BI --cfg " file"
Use an alternate config file.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-mouse
Disable all mouse backends.
.TP
.BI --mouse= auto|sgr|u1000|1002|1015|gpm|sysmouse
Force a mouse backend.
.TP
.BI --utf8= on|off
Force wide-character mode.
.TP
.BR \-\-version ", " \-V
Print version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-help ", " \-h
Print usage and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-dump\-license
Print the 2-clause BSD license and exit.
.SH INTERACTIVE KEYS
F10 or Alt activates the menubar; arrows navigate, Enter selects, Esc
backs out; mouse click opens a menu title and drag sweeps across titles.
In the Command window: Enter runs the line into the window's scrollback,
Ctrl+Up/Down walk the persisted history, Tab completes command names,
Ctrl+Y kills to end of line, Ctrl+S pauses, Esc aborts (SET ESCAPE).
Ctrl+F2 raises the Command window. Every window has a × close button on
its title bar (closing the Command window hides it; Ctrl+F2 brings it
back). Drag a window border to move it, the corner to resize it.
In a Browse window (M4): arrows/Tab move the cell cursor, Enter commits
and moves down, typing edits the cell, Esc cancels the edit or closes the
window, Ctrl+T toggles the delete mark, Ctrl+N appends a record; mouse
click positions, wheel scrolls, header drag reorders columns, border drag
resizes, double-click on a border sizes to widest.
QUIT or File > Quit exits with status 0.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/reynard/reynard.cfg
Configuration file (override with \fBREYNARD_CFG\fR or \fB--cfg\fR).
.TP
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/reynard/history
Command history (interactive mode).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B REYNARD_CFG
Config path override.
.TP
.B REYNARD_DATAPATH
Data file search path.
.TP
.B REYNARD_CODEPAGE
Default code page.
.TP
.B REYNARD_NOUPDATE
Open everything read-only (safety flag).
.TP
.B RX_LOG
Trace level: debug, info, warn, error.
.TP
.B TERM, COLORTERM, LANG, TMPDIR, TMUX, TERM_PROGRAM
Standard terminal/locale variables; only *.UTF-8 locales enable UTF-8 mode.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Script or runtime error.
.TP
.B 2
Usage or environment error.
.TP
.B 3
Lock conflict.
.TP
.B 4
Internal assertion (bug); writes \fBreynard-crash.log\fR.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B reynard -c '? "Hello:", 6*7'
Print a computed line in batch mode.
.TP
.B reynard -t demo.prg -o out.txt
Run a script deterministically, capturing output.
.TP
.B reynard -
Read commands from standard input.
.TP
.B reynard -t prog.prg
Run a script with procedures, loops and arrays; a byte-reproducible
compiled cache prog.rxp is written next to it and reused while the source
is unchanged.
.SH PACKAGING
Release artifacts (spec \u00a713): CPack DEB/RPM/TGZ/ZIP from a CMake build
dir, plus per-distribution recipes under \fIpackaging/\fR (Debian,
RPM, BSD ports, Homebrew, Alpine/musl static, macOS universal2 zip).
API documentation: \fImake docs\fR (Doxygen, build/docs/html), published
to the \fIdocs\fR branch by CI. Release tags M0..M10 and v1.0.0.
.SH SEE ALSO
Full language reference: \fIdocs/language.md\fR; file formats:
